[{"id":"rsync-predict-release","itemId":"reset-synchroniser","role":"core","promptHtml":"This is lesson 9.4's reset synchroniser, <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> has been 1 for a while, so <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is 1. <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> falls 2 ns after the edge that starts cycle 1. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> falls only at a rising edge, the second after <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> falls: <code class=\"nobreak\">r1</code> takes 0 at cycle 2's edge, and <code class=\"nobreak\">r2</code>, which drives <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code>, at cycle 3's. A reset that ended between edges ends, for every flip-flop on this clock, at one edge.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"rsync-release","source":"hdl/level-09/rst_sync/rst_sync_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":6,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"rst_sync_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"arst","path":"rst_sync_tb.arst","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1.2,"0"]]},{"label":"rst","path":"rst_sync_tb.rst","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[3,"0"]],"samples":["1","1","1","0","0","0"]}]},"answer":"rst"},{"id":"rsync-find-bug","itemId":"reset-synchroniser","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync_bug</code> should be lesson 9.4's <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code>: <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> rises as soon as <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> does, without waiting for <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code>. Its testbench, the one <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> passes, fails: <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> rose at 7 ns, and at 8 ns <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> is still X, not 1. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>The block runs only at rising edges of <code class=\"nobreak\">clk</code>, so it sees <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> at the next edge, not when it rises: the reset waits for the clock. It is lesson 2.3's mistake again, and it matters more here, because a reset may come while the clock is not running. With <code>or posedge arst</code>, the block also runs the moment <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> rises.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-09/rst_sync_bug/rst_sync_bug.sv","firstLine":10,"lines":[[{"text":"  (* ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"ASYNC_REG","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"\"TRUE\"","color":"var(--code-token-string-expression)","bold":false},{"text":" *)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":" logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" r1, r2;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"if","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (arst) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"      r1 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      r2 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"else","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"      r1 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1'b0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      r2 ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" r1;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" rst ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" r2;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"bugLine":12,"fixLine":"always_ff @(posedge clk or posedge arst) begin"},{"id":"rsync-report-fdpe","itemId":"reset-synchroniser","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">press_count_top</code> has a <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> for each of its two clocks, both set by BTN1. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report. An FDPE is a flip-flop with an asynchronous preset, an input that sets it to 1 at once, without the clock.","explanationHtml":"<p>4: the two flip-flops of each <code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">r1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">r2</code>, which <code class=\"nobreak\">arst</code> sets to 1 at once through their preset. The other flip-flops are FDREs, whose reset input, R, works only at a clock edge (lesson 2.3).</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/press_count/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":182,"excerpt":["+------------+------+---------------------+","|  Ref Name  | Used | Functional Category |","+------------+------+---------------------+","| FDRE       |   33 |        Flop & Latch |","| LUT4       |    9 |                 LUT |","| CARRY4     |    5 |          CarryLogic |","| OBUF       |    4 |                  IO |","| FDPE       |    4 |        Flop & Latch |","| IBUF       |    3 |                  IO |","| BUFG       |    3 |               Clock |","| LUT2       |    2 |                 LUT |","| LUT1       |    2 |                 LUT |","| MMCME2_ADV |    1 |               Clock |","| LUT5       |    1 |                 LUT |","| LUT3       |    1 |                 LUT |","+------------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many FDPE cells does press_count_top use?","answer":"4","numeric":true},{"id":"rsync-order-steps","itemId":"reset-synchroniser","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">rst_sync</code> turns BTN1 into <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> for one clock's domain. Put in order what happens with one press.","explanationHtml":"<p>The press sets both flip-flops at once, through their preset, so <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code> needs no edge. Letting go only allows them to take 0, at edges: <code class=\"nobreak\">r1</code> first, then <code class=\"nobreak\">r2</code>, which drives <code class=\"nobreak\">rst</code>. Any metastability from a release too close to an edge is in <code class=\"nobreak\">r1</code>, which has a whole cycle to settle before <code class=\"nobreak\">r2</code> takes it.</p>","type":"order","steps":["BTN1 is pressed: arst rises.","rst rises at once, with no clock edge.","BTN1 is let go: arst falls, between two edges.","At the next rising edge, r1 takes 0.","At the edge after that, r2 takes 0, and rst falls."],"shuffled":[1,4,2,0,3]}]